  "notes": [
    "These four stories are new holdout texts. They do not reuse Maya, Luca, Nadia, or the baseline letter/envelope/boat plot.",
    "The lighthouse token is already in the PR lexicon, so the out-of-lexicon places are named shops: la librairie Atlas, Harbottle's bookshop.",
    "Place precision for the pass bar excludes those two out-of-lexicon shops; they are reported separately.",
    "A bare 'vers'/'toward' plus a lexicon place is expected as an uncertain scene cut, not as a required gold scene. Firm (non-uncertain) false place changes count as false cuts.",
    "Scoring follows the baseline method: character and place precision/recall on names (case-insensitive, alias containment), strict scene-boundary recall on consecutive gold place changes, false cuts = API place changes that are not an expected boundary, excluding cuts marked uncertain when they match an expected toward-cue."
  ],
  "rules_summary": [
    "At most one scene cut per sentence. Several cues in the same sentence set the new scene once.",
    "A place change or a real time jump opens a new scene. A sequence word alone opens only a new shot in the current scene.",
    "No cut if the place or time does not actually change.",
    "Ignore false friends: a place only in dialogue or a memory does not cut; 'dans'/'in' without a place does not cut; a glance toward a street without leaving does not cut.",
    "A cue-only sentence with no action is not a scene and attaches to the next sentence.",
    "A bare vers/toward plus a real lexicon place is an uncertain scene cut, shown dashed, not a required gold scene.",
    "Places outside the closed lexicon, and not supplied as user places, may be missed. That known limit is measured on the two named shops."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "scene_boundary": "An expected scene boundary is a change of place or a real time jump between two consecutive expected scenes. Correct = expected place-to-place boundaries that also appear in the compressed API place sequence. Missed cut = expected boundary with no matching API change. False cut = a firm (not marked uncertain) API place change that does not match an expected boundary. Uncertain toward-cues are tallied separately.",
    "characters": "Precision and recall against gold_characters names (case-insensitive). Spurious names are false positives. The waiter/serveur is not a gold character. Atlas and Harbottle are not gold characters.",
    "places": "Precision and recall against gold_places aliases. Official pass-bar precision excludes out_of_lexicon places. A hit on a non_places name is a false positive. An uncertain toward-target (station/gare) that is not a gold scene is reported separately and, if present only as an uncertain cut, is not a precision false positive for the official bar; if it is promoted to a firm detected place, it is a false positive.",
    "pass_bar": {
      "all_http_200": true,
      "character_precision_micro": 0.9,
